A||N||6||gmata||Automatic Transmission problems.. HELP!!!||||11||
Z||000000||gmata||03-26-2001||11:26 PM||||Just got home and I can't put my car into gear.  It is stuck in Park.  Any ideas?  I haven't had problems with the transmission.  I checked the fluids and everything looks okay..  Need help..<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-26-2001||11:42 PM||||Two places to check, at the trans, and at the selector lever...<BR>Does the selector move, or is it locked?<BR>If it is locked, then check the anti theft cable from the ignition switch...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||03-26-2001||11:54 PM||||Did you turn the key to on? Did you push the lil button? try pushing forward on the shifter then back.. after doing the above two things. who knows?<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||03-27-2001||12:01 AM||||Is the car parked on a hill?  If its on a grade and put into park, the car will move slightly after the brakes are released.  This could cause the trans to get stuck in park also.  Just need to move the car back slightly to release the pressure on the trans and it should shift.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||03-27-2001||09:21 AM||||What Fformula88 says is true.  That's a good reason to always use the parking brake even in an automatic.  Plus that keeps the brakes adjusted and the cables from siezing up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||03-27-2001||12:26 PM||||Is there a lot of change sitting under your ash trays in the center console. It may be as high as the shift mechanism.<P>Hey it could happen!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||gmata||03-27-2001||01:10 PM||||Thanks guys.. It turned out to be the shift cable. ||||reg||14
